    {
      "id": "evt_gcal_com_verci_dfcbe905",
      "name": "creative parallel play",
      "type": "technology",
      "locationId": "",
      "communityId": "com_verci",
      "description": "Our creative book club is evolving :)\n\nAs we continue to grow as artists and practice the lessons in the book, I think it\u2019s time for this book club to evolve and transition into new formats:\nweekly co-creating session, where we work on our arts together and separately (think parallel play? But also small exercises to share with each other? skill sharing?)\nsometimes movie club? We can watch some movies together that inspire you to make art\nweekly show and tell + accountability for what we are working on\nfuture book club again (?) potential new titles include the creative act by Rick Rubin\ntopic of your choosing! Please feel free to propose and lead your own creative play session\nPlease also feel free to also invite other folks who might be interested in creating, crafting, or hanging out together. \n\nWe are meeting on Verci 9th floor in the couch area. \n\nFor this upcoming Monday, we are doing a bit of creative parallel play. Bring your own creative medium, or I will also bring some craft supplies with some generative prompts! see you soon :)",
