    {
      "id": "evt_gcal_com_verci_321bf0ec",
      "name": "Book Club: The Beauty of the Husband",
      "type": "technology",
      "locationId": "",
      "communityId": "com_verci",
      "description": "Monday, December 14, 7\u20139pm\nWe\u2019re reading The Beauty of the Husband: A Fictional Essay in 29 Tangos by Anne Carson.\nCarson is a Canadian poet and classicist who won the 2026 Nobel Prize in Literature. She writes about love and desire by pulling the ancient Greeks into the present, and this one is her take on a marriage, told as 29 tangos. It\u2019s short, and it\u2019s strange.\nPlease come having read the whole book. We\u2019ll be talking about all of it. Expect close reading and thematic analysis.\n\nWhat is marriage book club? An experimental social club for marriage, in New York City. Think book club, but for all kinds of media: books, film, TV, music, all kinds of media about what marriage is and what it does. Open to married, queer, engaged, long-term committed, or anyone who thinks about marriage. This is Edition 001.",
